        //
        // Note that the first node is the root. So the root must have a[root] >= X.
        // Then, from the root, we can go to any neighbor. But if a neighbor has a[neighbor] < X, we cannot visit it in the first k positions.
        // So effectively, we can only traverse within the connected component of nodes with a[i] >= X that contains the root.
        //
